sops.workflow:
1. User -> Transportation Planner;
2. Transportation Planner -> Accommodation Planner;
3. Accommodation Planner -> Restaurant Planner
   Accommodation Planner -> Attractions Planner (in parallel);
4. Restaurant Planner, Attractions Planner -> Final Plan Summarizer;
5. Final Plan Summarizer -> End.

Description:
First, the Transportation Planner determines the primary mode of transportation and establishes the location for each day of the trip, ensuring the Santa Ana-Texas-Santa Ana closed loop. The Transportation Planner must validate all transportation details (using FlightSearch for flights and GoogleDistanceMatrix for driving) against sandbox data to ensure accuracy before finalizing. This validated logistical framework is then passed to the Accommodation Planner to arrange child-friendly lodging. Afterwards, the plan is simultaneously passed to the Restaurant Planner and Attractions Planner, who work in parallel to find the best options in their respective areas while respecting the $5,800 budget. Once their individual plans are complete, the Final Plan Summarizer receives all information to generate a comprehensive and user-friendly final travel itinerary in the specified format.
